Dear Applicants,

We are writing to clarify an application requirement that has generated several inquiries.

All FY2026 Community Development Grant applications MUST include a self-assessment evaluation rubric as part of the application package. This requirement is stated in Section 4(e) of the Grant Guidelines but we want to ensure all applicants are aware.

The evaluation rubric should:
- Address each of the Foundation's five priority areas (see Guidelines Section 7)
- Include specific, measurable indicators for each priority area
- Describe the data collection methods for each indicator
- Establish baseline and target values where applicable

Applications submitted without an evaluation rubric will be considered incomplete and may not advance to full review.

If you have questions about rubric format or content, contact Dr. Amara Okafor at a.okafor@fieldstone-fdn.org.

